From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:11:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] input_origin: pin the room-plumbing rule to the
 resume rule; read only its 3 columns per submit

Follow-up to #1816 review nits (t_01a1d29d72344153, GitHub review 5884937401):

1. human_input._row_is_room_plumbing copies the plumbing rule (model_config.room_plumbing, or a hidden
   "Group:" row) from agent_factory._stored_session_runtime_overrides. That function is upstream code, so
   it stays untouched (no merge-conflict surface) and a parity test now runs both over one 420-row matrix
   (model_config dict/JSON text/invalid/list/null/blank x 7 titles x 5 hidden values; each row carries a
   stored model, so the resume rule restores a non-empty override unless it calls the row plumbing).
   Drift on either side fails it.
2. _stored_room_plumbing no longer calls db.get_session() on every would-be human submit (flush_for_read
   plus the system-prompt/tool-name JOINs on the request thread): it reads
   SELECT model_config, hidden, title FROM sessions WHERE id = ? and feeds that row to the same predicate.
   A missing row is a plain miss. Profile sessions still go through server._session_db (pooled
   hermes_state_registry.acquire handle).

Proof: RED on origin/main 3e6f010495 (narrow-read test: get_session/flush_for_read called; the parity
test is green on main since the copies agree today, and it kills drift mutants). GREEN: 12 files that
import human_input / input_origin, 197 passed. Mutants 8/8 killed (title strip, hidden ignored,
agent_factory case-folded Group and dropped model_config flag, back to get_session, no None-db guard,
no missing-row guard, SELECT *). scripts/check --base origin/main: 18 checks ok.
